  "structure": {
    "block_count": 87,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Best Pregnancy-Safe Hair Dye",
        "text_sha256": "cea4429a7b5c4b98a34bccd6d2d20acec5f3fcab2061905d264e60b83d4be018",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Best Hair Dye to Use",
        "text_sha256": "16aa96461fb2dbcf6483eee19ee442555c4353736b9696382541dcdc5718e35f",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Many first-time moms choose not to dye their hair while they’re pregnant. After all, hair dyes are made of pretty harsh chemicals, and if you’re already having to ditch natural stuff like raw fish and soft cheeses, it stands to reason that your salon appointments should also go on pause, right?",
        "text_sha256": "17476ca56506727e09fd8c10af48185366e9cbcaf6a7cd00a60a8c44474b382a",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Not so — many health experts say it’s safe to keep dyeing your hair while you’re pregnant. According to the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG) , hair dye and hair treatments are not dangerously toxic and are generally safe to use during pregnancy. Your skin also only absorbs a small amount of hair dye through the scalp, and the small amount of chemicals is unlikely to have any harmful effect. That said, most dermatologists recommend that expectant moms wait to dye their hair until after the first trimester, which is a critical period for development.",
        "text_sha256": "610aa61ce0bdcb5690e7bebd2c2fef436bf5c09aafdf62dca581c7e82bf547c0",
        "word_count": 97
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“Hair dyes do contain some ingredients that could be harmful in large amounts. However, the amount of hair dye you’ll use in a dyeing session would still be harmless,” says board-certified dermatologist Ife J. Rodney, M.D. , founding director of Eternal Dermatology + Aesthetics and professor of dermatology at Howard University and George Washington University. “Unless you work in cosmetology or you’re exposed to large amounts of dyes daily, hair dyes — both temporary and permanent — are safe to use.”",
        "text_sha256": "3d9b79ec151935a5e63869f9a8ef9c6f4192a582dec509ea02f09b806afbbcd0",
        "word_count": 81
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "However, you should still take some precautions to minimize any risks of causing harm to your developing baby.",
        "text_sha256": "3a4e16e04f727ab8ae0d47edb83e7da40b2b788f6bd85d40da42f24ac3c56b02",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What to look for in a pregnancy-safe hair dye",
        "text_sha256": "5621ee3ce38ce8284c080b13bdee984017eaa964dc3951702dc69a27a5edf1d8",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are a few factors that may make a hair dye safer during pregnancy than others. Those include products that are:",
        "text_sha256": "495aeb74c1ed1f142f954103b907c036155189dd2e6b46cb2197a3c131df3599",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Plant-based or organic. You may absorb more of the chemicals in hair dye if your scalp is irritated or infected, so invest in hair dye that is specifically labeled as having plant-based or organic ingredients — which might be gentler on your skin. ”Plant-based hair dyes containing henna or organic products are very popular. So you can use those while pregnant and switch to regular dyes after childbirth or breastfeeding,” Dr. Rodney says.",
        "text_sha256": "4d399a0e2b808509e6d27c2362ddfad992f8ffe718e72aaadadcfdd884cc8b07",
        "word_count": 73
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Free of certain irritants. Where possible, look for a product that doesn’t contain ammonia, heavy metals, parabens or phthalates, Dr. Rodney says. Why? Per the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) , high amounts of ammonia have been found in animal studies to affect a baby’s birth weight and size, although it’s unknown if those findings translate to humans, too. (There’s no evidence that environmental exposure to ammonia can cause birth defects, either — although the fumes can make you feel nauseous.) Exposure to heavy metals during pregnancy has been associated with miscarriages, birth defects and other health issues for babies. And parabens (common preservatives) and phthalates (which are used as solvents in products with fragrance) may potentially affect the reproductive system , although more conclusive research is needed. Because there’s so much unknown with these ingredients, many experts will say it’s better to be safe and avoid them.",
        "text_sha256": "2f6775073fe36158f00d9c43579b8b12f53dd1f1b9e1e03f6958e92639417150",
        "word_count": 150
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How to use hair dye safely during pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "fb8b11866df25ba5f988f1944ab6e18c005fbe3c9afa84a9897bbe6648169d58",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Dyeing your own hair at home inherently comes with some risks, regardless of whether you’re pregnant or not. To ensure that you don’t experience any negative side effects when coloring your hair (even when using an all-natural dye), Dr. Rodney recommends keeping the following in mind:",
        "text_sha256": "7c8c87754ecf31e279e128bfe3c9647c40c1651737bfce957f6486104ae4e09d",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Always do a patch test at home. Swab a small amount of product on an inconspicuous area on your body (like the inside of your arm) and monitor it for 48 hours to ensure you don’t have an allergic reaction. This can also be performed at your doctor’s office if you prefer the insight of a medical professional.",
        "text_sha256": "20e930e09c204516af4386605dbe588da07f199c846601e3137b147536ab24d0",
        "word_count": 58
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Dye your hair in a well-ventilated area. This limits the amount of fumes you breathe in, which can make you feel dizzy and sick. (Last thing you want while you’re pregnant.)",
        "text_sha256": "a4c78875f44a690a0a84afcf6fc4d68a2a312ce735c8d556a6c0705e760d070c",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Apply dye for the shortest amount of time to limit exposure to chemicals and fumes.",
        "text_sha256": "41e1fd8c9f36b1d78ecd57a7cb8cc6925f6a915904f6cc53f37fb2c68aa14ef5",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Use ointment on the skin around your hairline to limit skin exposure to the dye. (This also helps you avoid getting pigment on your forehead and skin when you’re applying.) Petroleum jelly or a thick moisturizer can do the trick.",
        "text_sha256": "a4f31bcf35622dbb9eb92d17e809e0f9b90382d4b66f4e0b2436a45cdff0bd21",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Read the instructions on the box before starting. Do not leave the chemicals on your hair any longer than indicated, and wash your scalp thoroughly after the treatment.",
        "text_sha256": "3c97560ff837f9d10ee26bd7ae281d265eb918fe73551ea8d39944b7f8decb08",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Avoid contact with skin and eyes. Wearing protective gloves can help with this.",
        "text_sha256": "47a47e1091ec4142afe67927bf9b38bd5ad177de5d82298baae8904b1888b272",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Don’t dye your hair if you have a skin infection. This can increase the amount of dye your skin absorbs.",
        "text_sha256": "586f6c29ab55b702d3623f0c24741c01b6868780b3a28e314d11279e6c0aabf2",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you work in a salon and you’re pregnant, you may want to take extra precautions to keep you and baby safe, since you’re exposed to hair dye and chemicals in the air for long periods of time. Be sure to wear gloves and take frequent fresh air breaks.",
        "text_sha256": "f0d29563cc5968bb47997755ca631cb9eb504717007b3eae637a0b7f1cbac859",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Of course, if you have concerns about the safety of your hair products or other hair treatment, consult your physician first.",
        "text_sha256": "c0d094c0c4856826690a32fb6ad2f392d9e7b4a912af3c821e2dd7fed86e0a70",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How we made our picks for the best pregnancy-safe hair dye",
        "text_sha256": "7bb4650a8dfb781cafcda578775ead25fb0065561e2b3f43e66cc741147d46b3",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "We made our selections for the best pregnancy-safe hair dye by looking for products that are plant-based and/or organic and free of certain ingredients as outlined in the guidance above. We also consulted What to Expect community and user reviews to make sure we were picking the best of the best.",
        "text_sha256": "5225123a9cf970dccff7a8b64996e5f3c74fc3f6b5d1ce15dad19897ca213e20",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Best Budget-Friendly Option",
        "text_sha256": "bd8c5337f665362c1d19f69f79f11c6e0117b19afb2fe7875baeca9920a1b28e",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Garnier Olia Ammonia-Free Hair Color",
        "text_sha256": "9af510999196a93e927d0364f93ba417e4efaa22b3f857879435db40b10d9512",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "More affordable than other dyes",
        "text_sha256": "b4900b0ed4446fcb492d8a3fed6730d3ec96191378dea7e97a152d30da3f7e99",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "no strong odor",
        "text_sha256": "611e6ebd5edb02db2fe5128baab9941b9c9ef443d897c6be8565b69378ee24a3",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Some people say the color didn’t look as advertised",
        "text_sha256": "4954e7a68b0b6370669e4859ab6441b5db27fa2ee6cf1385f6f582de0e1234f8",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Why We Love It",
        "text_sha256": "6e31e7604a2268d00ddf2594453e493aef84f8dd297f3a72433e60834fa4117b",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This ammonia-free hair dye is formulated with 60 percent natural oils. It stands out from most hair colors because the oil is concentrated within the colorant to boost the coloring process and make your hair color more vibrant. Garnier Olia can be used to touch up your roots or do an all-over color. It’s also available in 34 shades (including fun ones like rose gold and silver), so it’s easy to find exactly the color you’re looking for. Reviewers love that it's made of natural oils so hair is left feeling soft and smooth, and has a pleasant scent (no ammonia, means no gross ammonia smell!).",
        "text_sha256": "d3805abc3a789c5d9b54d59775a5f2098a3750b44b1a5ba9ed326d9b464278d3",
        "word_count": 106
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Applications per box: 1",
        "text_sha256": "95b344b8b3c3589c04ae3feff0504a6a836c5d418fc5aeef9817c1715560d5f9",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Best Natural Hair Dye",
        "text_sha256": "e61736ae71d96491ae2c91097f08422ce3920f09f19bc9376a8d841c54400183",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "ONC Natural Colors Healthier Permanent Hair Color",
        "text_sha256": "5c93913b45bc3b2e719ba544a8b3850a8710242c308c5c953adf39ca4a2efdb9",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
